==English==
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
{{PIE word|en|tréyes}}
From {{inh|en|enm|tribe}}, {{m|enm|tribu}}, from {{der|en|fro|tribu}}, from {{der|en|la|tribus}}. {{doublet|en|tribus}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/tɹaɪb/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-tribe.ogg|a=US}}
* {{rhymes|en|aɪb|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# {{lb|en|history|anthropology}} An [[ethnic group]] larger than a [[band]] or [[clan]] (and which may contain clans) but smaller than a [[nation]] (and which in turn may be contained within a nation). The tribe is often the basis of ethnic identity.
#: {{ux|en|the Twelve '''Tribes''' of Israel;&emsp;Germanic&nbsp;'''tribes''';&emsp;Celtic&nbsp;'''tribes'''}}
#: ''The Formation of Kazakh Identity: From '''Tribe''' to Nation-state''
# {{lb|en|synecdoche}} A [[tribal]] nation or people.
# {{lb|en|pejorative}} A nation or people in an area considered culturally primitive, such as Africa, Australia or [[Native America]].
# A [[social]]ly [[cohesive]] group of [[people]] within a [[society]].
#* {{quote-book|1=en|year=2005|author=w:Sean Dooley|title=The Big Twitch|publisher=Allen and Unwin|location=Sydney|page=26|passage=The thought of spending a year in close company with twitchers chilled me to the core. Not that I have anything against them, I am terribly fond of the members of the '''tribe''', it is just that basically, they are a bunch of obsessive freaks.}}
# A [[class]] or [[group]] of [[thing]]s.
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1972|author={{w|Carol A. Nemeyer}}|title=Scholarly Reprint Publishing in the United States|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=w:R. R. Bowker Co.|isbn=0835204855|page=7|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/scholarlyreprint0000neme_h4x8/page/6/mode/2up?q=tribe|passage=In 1968, estimates of the number of active reprint publishers ranged from about 20 to 100 publishers. The fact that almost 300 U.S. reprint publishers have been identified is evidence that the reprint '''tribe''' continues to increase.}}
# {{lb|en|zoology}} A group of [[ape]]s who live and work together.
# {{lb|en|taxonomy}} A hierarchal rank between [[family]] and [[genus]].
# A group of affiliated [[Mardi Gras Indian]]s.
# {{n-g|The [[collective noun]] for various animals.}}
# {{lb|en|stock breeding}} A family of animals descended from some particular [[female]] [[progenitor]], through the female line.
#: {{ux|en|the Duchess '''tribe''' of shorthorns}}

